{"org":"elastic","repo":"elasticsearch","prNumber":"119134","commit":"a8335f79231c049065b5445bdac41e60c751c503","generatedCommentsNodes":[{"comment":"The addition of `FieldMapper.IGNORE_MALFORMED_SETTING.getKey()` to the settings builder is correct and consistent with how other settings are handled. However, ensure that this setting does not inadvertently affect the downsampled index in a way that contradicts the purpose or expected behavior of downsampling.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java-x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java--43574:43884","promptId":"#ZSR2N","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","srcChanges":[],"dstChanges":[{"pos":43574,"endPos":43884,"startLine":904,"startLineOffset":8,"endLine":909,"endLineOffset":9,"length":311}]}]},{"comment":"The addition of `ignore_malformed` to the mapping and settings is consistent across the diffs, but it\u0027s important to ensure that this setting is appropriate for all use cases where downsampled indices are created. If `ignore_malformed` is not relevant or could lead to data loss or unexpected behavior in some scenarios, it should be conditionally added based on specific criteria.","nodes":[{"id":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java-x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java--34566:34726","promptId":"#ZFNH6","srcPath":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","dstPath":"x-pack/plugin/downsample/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/downsample/TransportDownsampleAction.java","src